You have a Java application running inside a Docker container on a VM. If the process has one PID inside the container and another PID on the host, which PiD is greater and why?



1.The host PID is always greater than the container PID 

2.Inside the container, the namespace creates a isolated environment where our Java application thinks it is the only major process running, assigning it PID 1 (or a very low number).

3.On the host, the process is viewed as part of the entire system's global process tree. Since the host has been running many system processes, daemons, and services.

4.The host tracks every process across the entire virtual machine consecutively, the global counter will almost always be much higher than the isolated, freshly initialized counter inside the container.



